Do not use the unsigned 6809 MUL instruction for signed widening products.
Drop the invalid mulqihi3 pattern so GCC widens operands and uses ordinary
HImode multiplication instead. Keep the zero-extending umulqihi3 pattern.
Regression: tests/cases/mulqihi3_signed.c and run_signed_mul_review.py.

--- a/gcc/config/m6809/m6809.md
+++ b/gcc/config/m6809/m6809.md
@@ -956,12 +956,3 @@
-; TODO - merge these two instructions, using 'extend_operator' to match
-; either signed or zero extension.  Everything else is the same.
-(define_insn "mulqihi3"
-   [(set (match_operand:HI 0 "register_operand" "=d")
-      (mult:HI (sign_extend:HI (match_operand:QI 1 "general_operand" "%q"))
-      (match_operand:QI 2 "general_operand" "tmK")))]
-  ""
-  "lda\t%2\t;mulqihi3\;mul"
-  [(set_attr "length" "3")])
-
-
+; MUL is unsigned. Signed byte operands must widen before HI multiplication;
+; only the zero-extending pattern can use this instruction directly.
 (define_insn "umulqihi3"
